# Debounce vs throttle

Both tame a noisy event stream, but they answer different questions.
Debounce answers "has the user stopped?"; it waits for a quiet gap
before firing. Throttle answers "what is happening right now?"; it
fires at a steady cadence while events keep coming.

<Figure caption="The same burst of events (top), debounced (middle), throttled (bottom).">
